Ticket #4471 contains reports for two different date problems. The export has overlapping
pages, so count each report ID once. Classify by the tenant's date order, booking form, and
intake channel; the browser's intake tag is not the cause.

## Date parser reads day-first dates as month-first

The shared parser treats the month as the first part of every date. For tenants whose locale
writes the day first, the parser can swap the day and month. This affects app and email
reports, and form reports for the `booking-v2` form.

## Booking form hint conflicts with tenant date order

The `booking-v3` form tells people to enter dates month first, but the form reads them using
the tenant's day-first locale. A form report from a `booking-v3` tenant therefore has a
different cause from a parser report, even though both can show a swapped date.

## Re-triage

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

The desk merged both causes into one known ticket. Track them separately so each issue has
one cause and one report count. The cause table deduplicates report IDs and derives each
count from the exported records. Some intake tags disagree with the tenant and channel data,
so do not use those tags to split the work.

